steps.explanation:
Now for the solution! useCallback memoizes a function, returning the same function reference across re-renders unless dependencies change.

Syntax:
```tsx
const memoizedFn = useCallback(() => {
  // function code
}, [dependencies])
```

With an empty dependency array [], the function never changes. When you wrap handleLog with useCallback, React.memo will see it's the same function reference and LogButton won't re-render!

steps.task:
1. Import useCallback from 'react'
2. Wrap handleLog with useCallback and an empty dependency array:

const handleLog = useCallback(() => {
  console.log('Button was clicked!')
}, [])

Test: Click 'Increment Counter' - LogButton no longer re-renders! (No 'LogButton rendered' logs)
